{"compatibility":"minor","safety_note_md":"# SafeStan Safety Note

Compatibility: minor.

Protected data: `r0`, `r1`.

Generated files: `model_safe.stan`, `data_safe.json`.

Changes: reordered the model block so all top-level parameters (`b`, `mu`, `alpha`, `beta1`, `beta2`, and `sigma_sq`) receive their built-in prior sampling statements before they are used in likelihood terms. This preserves the same posterior/log density because Stan sampling statements add commutative log-density contributions. No data changes were required.
","model_safe_stan":"// http://www.mrc-bsu.cam.ac.uk/bugs/winbugs/Vol1.pdf
// Page 34: Oxford: smooth fit to log-odds ratios

data {
  int<lower=0> K;
  array[K] int<lower=0> n0;
  array[K] int<lower=0> n1;
  array[K] int<lower=0> r0;
  array[K] int<lower=0> r1;
  vector[K] year;
}
transformed data {
  vector[K] yearsq;
  yearsq = year .* year;
}
parameters {
  vector[K] mu;
  real alpha;
  real beta1;
  real beta2;
  real<lower=0> sigma_sq;
  vector[K] b;
}
transformed parameters {
  real<lower=0> sigma;
  sigma = sqrt(sigma_sq);
}
model {
  b ~ normal(0, 1);
  mu ~ normal(0, 1000);
  alpha ~ normal(0.0, 1000);
  beta1 ~ normal(0.0, 1000);
  beta2 ~ normal(0.0, 1000);
  sigma_sq ~ inv_gamma(0.001, 0.001);

  r0 ~ binomial_logit(n0, mu);
  r1 ~ binomial_logit(n1,
                      alpha + mu + beta1 * year + beta2 * (yearsq - 22)
                      + b * sigma);
}
","data_safe_json":"{"K":2,"n0":[4,1],"n1":[2,4],"r0":[4,1],"r1":[2,4],"year":[4.240974931676864,2.1499331775085975]}","protected_variables":["r0","r1"]}
